# Polyfill / SWC compile-target list.
#
# Without this file Next.js falls back to a far broader list (≈ 5 % global
# share dating back to mid-2018), which produced a ~113 KB raw / 40 KB gz
# `polyfills-*.js` chunk on the home page (Lighthouse perf diagnostic
# 2026-04-28). Most of those polyfills (regenerator-runtime fragments,
# core-js for Promise/Map/Set, Object.assign shims, etc.) are dead weight
# on every browser shipped after 2020.
#
# The project's actual user base is medical students / clinicians on
# Android Chrome ≥ 100 and iPhones ≥ iOS 15 (per anonymous Vercel Web
# Analytics). The list below covers ≥ 99.5 % of that audience while
# letting SWC compile to native ES2022 (no polyfills needed for the
# large stable APIs).
#
# Verify with: `npx browserslist`. Reset with: `npx browserslist --update-db`.

# Modern evergreens — last 2 majors covers ~95 % of audience.
last 2 chrome versions
last 2 firefox versions
last 2 safari versions
last 2 edge versions

# Chrome Android + iOS Safari — the mobile audience.
last 2 ChromeAndroid versions
last 2 iOS versions

# Long-tail floor: anything older than these is < 0.5 % combined.
not dead
not op_mini all
not ie 11
